238	<h2><span class="num">4</span>Since 10-04: the skills and the process</h2>
239	<p class="lead"><strong>The process-engineering study</strong> (opened 10-03) asks whether the weekly token pool is spent well.</p>
240	<ul>
241	<li>Sharing one build between checkouts had been called impossible for two weeks. Given the goal, fresh agents found the way in about 15 minutes. The waste was 245 of 425 builds, about 7.3 agent-hours.</li>
242	<li>One probe wrote 7.0M tokens against an estimate of 0.5M. Now the coordinator watches a long run against its estimate.</li>
243	<li>Six designs for running batch 10 were priced: four at 4.5M to 7.5M, two with no cost limit at about 31M and 37M. Whether to design a workflow for each batch waits on the curator.</li>
244	<li>Next: redesign the round after a skeptic refuses.</li>
245	</ul>
246	<p class="lead"><strong>The <code>fortress-repo</code> skill</strong>: the instructions every agent loads to work here.</p>
247	<ul>
248	<li>10-04: three project skills written from the record and reviewed.</li>
249	<li>10-05: a reader given only the skill found about 30 passages a new reader could not act on.</li>
250	<li>10-05 and 10-06: the curator reviewed it, about 35 comments, grouped as eight lenses. A writer applied them, and every file got shorter.</li>
251	<li>10-07: the skill gained two modes of work, building and exploring.</li>
252	<li>10-08: a fresh session answered a quiz on Fortress from pre-training alone; an audit graded 56 claims correct, 7 wrong, 3 outdated. The section "Fortress as a language" came from it.</li>
253	</ul>
254	<p class="lead"><strong>The context study</strong> (10-08): what batch 10's four rung workers read before their first fix.</p>
255	<ul>
256	<li>Of what they read: the briefing 25%; code, library, specification and tests 48%; their own searches of the record 4%.</li>
257	<li>Relearning what the record held was common but small: about 1% of what they read.</li>
258	<li>A "librarian" pass after each batch would cost 0.7M to 0.9M tokens. It pays if it turns the causes of refusals into skill rules.</li>
259	</ul>
260	<h3>The ledger</h3>
261	<ul>
262	<li>An archaeology (10-08) proposed a form. The curator decided: one status word of seven, a class with its area, at most 1.2K characters a row, topic sections with every number kept, the old text in a history file, one tool, <code>ledger.py</code>, to write it.</li>
263	<li>The ledger check (10-08) compared about 490 rows with the batch records and found three mismatches.</li>
264	<li>The ledger rewrite is running now: one agent groups the rows by topic and spots duplicates, a rewriter takes each group, a merge agent writes the ledger. Estimate: 2.5M tokens, 3.5 hours.</li>
265	</ul>
266	<p class="lead"><strong>The climb</strong> has been paused since 10-03. Batch 11 is not drafted.</p>
