99	<div class="intro">
100	<p>Words used throughout:</p>
101	<dl class="gloss">
102	<div><dt>team</dt><dd>Designers of Fortress at Sun Labs, later Oracle Labs. Their last commit is <code>a874948ac</code> (2012-08-31).</dd></div>
103	<div><dt>type group</dt><dd>Part of the team that designed the type system and built the compiled type checker.</dd></div>
104	<div><dt>walk</dt><dd>Interpreter. It runs a program with no static types.</dd></div>
105	<div><dt>compiled path</dt><dd>Path that compiles a program to JVM bytecode and runs it: <code>fortress compile</code>, then <code>fortress run</code>.</dd></div>
106	<div><dt>checker</dt><dd>Static type checker. It runs on the compiled path only.</dd></div>
107	<div><dt>library</dt><dd>Fortress code that every program loads. There were two. The interpreter's is <strong>the one library</strong>. The compiler's own smaller one is <strong>the prelude</strong>.</dd></div>
108	<div><dt>switch-over</dt><dd>Point at which the compiled path moves onto the one library and the prelude is deleted. It comes when the checker accepts the one library.</dd></div>
109	<div><dt>record</dt><dd>Files under <code>explorations/</code> that hold what the revival has established (<code>FACTS.md</code>), what the curator decided (<code>POSITIONS.md</code>) and the plan (<code>PLAN.md</code>).</dd></div>
110	<div><dt>gap ledger</dt><dd>File with one numbered row for each known gap or defect.</dd></div>
