249	<p class="lead"><strong>Where the tokens went.</strong> "Written" means tokens processed fresh: cache writes and new input, the measure the curator uses.</p>
250	<ul>
251	<li>The 15 batches from the repair batch to 6.5b used 269 agents and wrote 146M tokens.</li>
252	<li>Rung workers took about half; skeptics, judges, repairs and reviews about two-fifths.</li>
253	<li>45% of all writes came after an agent waited five minutes or more. The prompt cache lives five minutes, so the agent wrote its whole context again.</li>
254	<li>The largest batches: 7 (22M), N (18M), 6.5b (17M). After the post-mortem: 7b 7.3M, 8 and 9 14.6M together, 10 6.3M.</li>
255	</ul>
256	<h3>Where the records went: the post-mortem of 09-29</h3>
257	<ul>
