288	<li>Sharing one build between checkouts had been called impossible for two weeks. Given the goal, fresh agents found the way in about 15 minutes. The waste was 245 of 425 builds, about 7.3 agent-hours.</li>
289	<li>One probe wrote 7.0M tokens against an estimate of 0.5M. Now the coordinator watches a long run against its estimate.</li>
290	<li>Six designs for running batch 10 were priced: four at 4.5M to 7.5M, two with no cost limit at about 31M and 37M. The study's close found nothing that more agents would fix (part 7).</li>
291	<li>On 10-08 the batch workflow was redesigned. The skeptic fixes what it finds, a judge rules only on a contested fix, and there's no second skeptic. Briefs shrank to a third to a ninth of their old size.</li>
292	</ul>
293	<p class="lead"><strong>The <code>fortress-repo</code> skill</strong>: the instructions every agent loads to work here.</p>
294	<ul>
295	<li>10-04: three project skills written from the record and reviewed.</li>
